WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.040
Is "Thor: Love and Thunder" Chris&nbsp;
Hemsworth's Marvel swan song?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.400
Or will he live to bring the hammer down&nbsp;
once again? And which comics should you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:10.160
read to get hyped up for the newest MCU&nbsp;
installment? For all of this and more,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.720
you'll want to watch this before&nbsp;
you see "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.360
In a universe where COVID-19 never happened, we&nbsp;
would have already seen "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:23.120
by now. At 2019's San Diego Comic-Con, Kevin Feige&nbsp;
revealed during the Marvel Studios panel that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.240
fourth "Thor" film would premiere on November&nbsp;
5, 2021. Thanks to delays from the pandemic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:32.720
that date ended up going to "Eternals." "Thor:&nbsp;
Love and Thunder" was pushed back multiple times,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.600
first to February 18, 2022. Shortly after that&nbsp;
switch, The Hollywood Reporter revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.800
the movie was bumping up one week earlier to&nbsp;
February 11. But Marvel Studios wasn't done yet.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.200
According to Variety, "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;
was moved to May 6, the eventual release date of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.240
"Doctor Strange in the Multiverse of Madness,"&nbsp;
before finally landing on July 8. This date is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.320
as set in stone as it ever will be, so mark&nbsp;
your calendars for the second Friday of July.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:00.800
As if there were any doubt, Chris Hemsworth&nbsp;
is returning in "Thor: Love and Thunder" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:05.440
play the titular hero. This marks the Aussie's&nbsp;
ninth MCU film appearance, which includes his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.280
small cameo in "Doctor Strange." While&nbsp;
that's a whopping amount of MCU flicks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:14.320
it still puts him behind Stan Lee with 22,&nbsp;
Samuel L. Jackson and Chris Evans with 11,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:18.080
and Robert Downey Jr. with 10 for&nbsp;
the most MCU movie appearances.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.240
If Hemsworth is to be taken at his word, "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.840
Love and Thunder" will not be his retirement&nbsp;
movie. In an interview with Elle Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.080
the actor joked that his character is far too&nbsp;
young for him to consider leaving the MCU.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:31.440
"Are you crazy?! I'm not going into any&nbsp;
retirement period (laughs). Thor is far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.640
too young for that. [He] is only&nbsp;
1500 years old! It is definitely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.840
not a film that I say goodbye to&nbsp;
this brand. At least I hope so."

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.160
We don't think anyone would be&nbsp;
disappointed to have Hemsworth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:42.480
stick around in the MCU for as long as possible.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.800
While Chris Hemsworth's return in "Thor: Love&nbsp;
and Thunder" is to be expected, the announcement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.040
that Natalie Portman would be returning to the&nbsp;
MCU in the film was more of a shock. The news&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:56.480
of the actress's return came during the Marvel&nbsp;
Studios panel at San Diego Comic-Con in 2019.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.320
While on stage, director Taika Waititi&nbsp;
introduced Portman to the Hall H crowd,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.000
saying she was the only person who could play&nbsp;
the female Thor in "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:08.000
Portman's last MCU appearance came in&nbsp;
"Avengers: Endgame," although she never actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.200
showed up to the set during production&nbsp;
on that movie. For her appearance there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.360
old footage of Jane Foster was recycled&nbsp;
from "Thor: The Dark World." That movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.840
"Thor's" first sequel, marks the last time Portman&nbsp;
filmed for Marvel Studios, as she did not appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:24.320
in "Thor: Ragnarok." Her absence in that film&nbsp;
is briefly explained in an offhand reference.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:25.600
"Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:31.120
"She didn't dump me. I dumped&nbsp;
her. It was a mutual dumping."

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.720
Variety reported the off-screen reason was&nbsp;
that Portman was disappointed with "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:38.880
The Dark World," and less-than-happy when&nbsp;
original director Patty Jenkins left the project.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.160
Regardless, the past is the past, and presumably,&nbsp;
money talks. Regardless of how they got her there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.720
Portman is back and better than&nbsp;
ever in "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.040
"Thor: Love and Thunder" will be Tessa&nbsp;
Thompson's third go-round as Valkyrie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.280
after debuting in "Thor: Ragnarok" and fighting&nbsp;
at the Battle of Earth in "Avengers: Endgame."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:59.600
The last we saw of Valkyrie was after Thanos&nbsp;
was defeated in the fourth "Avengers" film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:03.200
She says goodbye to Thor, who informally&nbsp;
declares her the new king of Asgard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:06.720
At the Marvel Studios panel at&nbsp;
San Diego Comic-Con in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.800
Thompson revealed that one of Valkyrie's first&nbsp;
orders of business would be to find her queen.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.400
This makes Valkyrie's return in "Thor:&nbsp;
Love and Thunder" all the more important.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.320
Thompson noted her excitement about this plot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:19.680
point when catching up with The Wrap&nbsp;
earlier this year. The actor said,

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:24.720
"We talk so much about representation and&nbsp;
obviously, in terms of the LGBTQIA community,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.120
there's still so much work&nbsp;
to be done. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:30.640
there's not a lot of time invested in love&nbsp;
stories in Marvel movies in general. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:33.360
that will be a little different on&nbsp;
the new 'Thor,' which is exciting."

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:39.360
In January 2020, Collider reported Christian Bale&nbsp;
was in talks to join "Thor: Love and Thunder." 11&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.600
months later, Marvel Studios confirmed on Twitter&nbsp;
that the Academy Award winner would be portraying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.840
the villainous comic character Gorr the God&nbsp;
Butcher. The actor has stayed silent on his role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:52.000
in the upcoming film, which has only heightened&nbsp;
the mystery of his character. Taika Waititi had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.320
some interesting comments regarding Bale's&nbsp;
Gorr, however. He told the Associated Press,

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.800
"In my humble opinion, we have probably the best&nbsp;
villain that Marvel's ever had in Christian Bale."

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:04.800
While the news of Bale joining an MCU project&nbsp;
might have seemed shocking to some fans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.080
the actor's resume proves he won't&nbsp;
shy away from a superhero flick.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:11.920
The actor famously played Batman in Christopher&nbsp;
Nolan's highly-praised "Dark Knight" trilogy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.360
from 2005 to 2012. Bale was lauded for his&nbsp;
portrayal of the Caped Crusader and Bruce Wayne.

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:24.080
"It's not who I am underneath,&nbsp;
but what I do that defines me."

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.800
"Thor: Love and Thunder" will show&nbsp;
us Bale on the opposite side of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.440
superhero spectrum, playing one heck of a baddie.

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:34.320
Specific plot points of "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;
are being kept under wraps, but we can make some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:38.480
educated guesses about what might happen in&nbsp;
the film based on the Marvel Comics lore. Gorr&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:43.920
first debuted in 2012's "Thor: God of Thunder #2"&nbsp;
making him a relatively new character considering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:49.360
Thor was created in 1962. Gorr had it rough:&nbsp;
he grew up on a nameless planet in deplorable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.760
conditions and was told his whole life that the&nbsp;
gods would provide for him, but they never did.

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:57.920
Everyone close to Gorr dies tragically,&nbsp;
including his parents, partner, and children.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:02.800
After living in such devastation, he assumes there&nbsp;
is no such thing as gods and gives up on the idea.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:07.040
One day, he comes across two of them battling when&nbsp;
they land on his planet. Knowing they're real,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:11.200
he makes it his mission to destroy every&nbsp;
last one of them. He successfully kills many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.640
and battles Thor on several occasions,&nbsp;
but this is where it gets interesting.

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:18.320
Gorr can travel the timestream thanks&nbsp;
to obtaining the blood of the Time Gods.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:21.440
This allows him to battle different&nbsp;
Thors all across the time stream,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:25.600
which makes Gorr a pretty intimidating threat&nbsp;
for any number of Thors to face in the new film.

00:05:26.560 --> 00:05:29.680
According to Deadline, Russell Crowe's&nbsp;
involvement in "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.440
was supposed to be a secret. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
the actor was spotted out one too many times&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:37.760
in Australia with several other cast members,&nbsp;
and the cat was out of the bag. His inclusion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:42.480
in the film was confirmed in March 2021, and his&nbsp;
role was later revealed by the actor himself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.800
While chatting with an Australian radio show,&nbsp;
Crowe said he had to leave to head to a studio.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:51.760
"Now, I'm gonna get on my bicycle, I'm gonna ride&nbsp;
up to Disney-Fox studios ... and round about 9:15,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:55.680
I shall be Zeus in 'Thor 4.' It's&nbsp;
my last day of Zeus-ing about."

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:00.240
Like Christian Bale, Crowe's entrance into&nbsp;
the MCU is preceded by time working on a DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.240 --> 00:06:05.600
project. The Oscar-winning actor played Jor-El,&nbsp;
the father of Superman in 2013's "Man of Steel."

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:09.120
We're not sure how big of a role Zeus will&nbsp;
play in "Thor: Love and Thunder," but Crowe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:13.280
certainly seems to enjoy playing the character.&nbsp;
The actor changed his Twitter avatar shortly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.720
after the film's first official trailer&nbsp;
dropped, with a screenshot of him as Zeus.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:22.800
This fourth "Thor" solo movie isn't that much of&nbsp;
a "solo" affair. Like many MCU sequels before it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:27.280
"Love and Thunder" serves as a superfriend team-up&nbsp;
of sorts. "Thor: Love and Thunder" will feature a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:31.200
majority of the Guardians of the Galaxy. When&nbsp;
we last saw the team, they were in the Benatar&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:35.600
after the Battle of Earth in "Avengers: Endgame."&nbsp;
Thor joined them on board, where he and Star Lord&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:40.000
argued over who was in charge. The Asgardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy were born, and for all we know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.440
Thor has been traveling across the&nbsp;
universe with his new pals in the meantime.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.760
Based on what we see in the&nbsp;
trailer and teaser for the film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:50.640
it looks like all the Guardians are back except&nbsp;
for Gamora. The galaxy's deadliest assassin is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:55.440
currently in hiding after time traveling&nbsp;
from 2014 to 2023 in "Avengers: Endgame."

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.480
That said, don't expect the Guardians&nbsp;
to take center stage in "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.840
Love and Thunder," as it's suspected they&nbsp;
will play a role in just the first act.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.280
Another former "Thor" and "Thor: The Dark World"&nbsp;
star is returning after missing "Thor: Ragnarok."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:11.040
Deadline broke the news of Jaimie Alexander's&nbsp;
inclusion in "Thor: Love and Thunder" in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:15.520
December 2020, revealing that the actress&nbsp;
was returning to the franchise as Lady Sif.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:20.080
While Alexander has been on a lengthy break from&nbsp;
the MCU, she did return as Sif in Episode 4 of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:24.640
"Loki," when Loki is forced to relive one moment&nbsp;
from his life over and over again on a time loop.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:29.520
Alexander also voiced Lady Sif in Episodes&nbsp;
3 and 7 of the Disney+ series "What If...?"

00:07:29.520 --> 00:07:33.440
After Episode 4 of "Loki" aired, Alexander&nbsp;
took to Instagram to proudly declare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:37.200
Lady Sif was back, adding that&nbsp;
she was here to stay. Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.200 --> 00:07:41.280
Whether Lady Sif will actually stick around past&nbsp;
"Thor: Love and Thunder" remains to be seen.

00:07:42.476 --> 00:07:46.880
And that's not all. In July 2021, Matt&nbsp;
Damon confirmed his own return to the MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:51.040
during an appearance on The Jess Cagle Show.&nbsp;
Following up on a hilarious scene from "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:53.520
Ragnarok" in which he played&nbsp;
an actor portraying Loki,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:57.040
he'll be joined by Luke Hemsworth as&nbsp;
the actor portraying Thor. Turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.040 --> 00:08:01.120
their one-off cameo appearances in the third&nbsp;
"Thor" movie won't be one-offs after all.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:04.720
"We had a ball, and so Taika&nbsp;
had us back again, to kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.280
run that joke back and upgrade it a little bit."

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.120
Also returning is Sam Neill, who&nbsp;
played Actor Odin in "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:15.680
An unofficial "Thor: Love&nbsp;
and Thunder" Twitter account,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:19.440
not endorsed by Marvel Studios, has already&nbsp;
shared some leaked set photos which showed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:23.120
the "Jurassic Park" actor in full Odin&nbsp;
gear. With these three stars returning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:23.120 --> 00:08:27.840
we suspect we'll get another Asgardian play — this&nbsp;
time perhaps about the events of "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:30.480
"I think they sussed out, because&nbsp;
paparazzi took pictures of us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.240
so that they sussed out what we were doing."

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:36.400
If they're recounting "Thor: Ragnarok," that&nbsp;
means they'd need a Hela. While still unconfirmed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:40.240
it looks like none other than Melissa McCarthy&nbsp;
will be playing the role of Hela's actor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.720
The Daily Mail shared photos&nbsp;
of the actress on the "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:46.240
Love and Thunder" set sporting a costume&nbsp;
that looks an awful lot like Hela's.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:50.320
These photos landed three months after McCarthy&nbsp;
and her husband, Ben Falcone, shared a pretend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:54.480
audition tape on Instagram asking Taika Waititi&nbsp;
if they could be in "Thor: Love and Thunder."

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.160
"Thor: Love and Thunder…"

00:08:56.160 --> 00:09:00.000
"We could be love and thunder…"

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.880
Naturally, Taika Waititi is back in the director's&nbsp;
chair for "Thor: Love and Thunder." The filmmaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:10.240
became a household name after revitalizing the&nbsp;
"Thor" franchise with "Thor: Ragnarok" in 2017.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:14.240
Waititi managed to bring color, laughter,&nbsp;
and a solid story to the Asgardian world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.040
which makes his return to "Thor 4" no surprise.

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:19.360
Waititi is approaching "Love&nbsp;
and Thunder" differently than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.840
"Ragnarok" though. When catching&nbsp;
up with Entertainment Weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.840 --> 00:09:26.320
the director admitted he didn't want to make the&nbsp;
same MCU film a second time. The filmmaker said,

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:30.400
"'Ragnarok' felt a bit like a party. It&nbsp;
was quite festive. This one is still fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:34.160
and it's got moments of being over the top, but&nbsp;
thematically, it's about something a bit deeper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:39.040
than the last film. It's not a serious film, and&nbsp;
it's not a drama, but we do deal with ideas that I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:43.520
think a lot of humans deal with — universal themes&nbsp;
about love and loss and our place in the world."

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:47.120
He also noted that his experience with his&nbsp;
first MCU film allowed him to shoot "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.120 --> 00:09:49.120
Love and Thunder" in a much more efficient way.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.360
"The whole thing's a f—ing mess, Taika."

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.520
Waititi also returns in the film as Korg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:56.320
the lovable Kronan we met on&nbsp;
Sakaar in "Thor: Ragnarok."

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:59.840
"Is that some sort of protoplasm, all&nbsp;
the stuff that's coming out of you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:03.817
or are they eggs? It looks like eggs."

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:07.920
The first "Thor: Love and Thunder" teaser&nbsp;
dropped in April 2022 and briefly touched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:12.320
on what's been going on with Thor since we last&nbsp;
saw him. We got a brief shot of Bro Thor with his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:16.720
massive beer belly exercising with chains while&nbsp;
sporting a "Strongest Avengers" trucker hat.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:21.040
It looks like he sheds the weight with ease, as&nbsp;
the rest of the teaser shows him in tip-top shape.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.600
The Guardians of the Galaxy are&nbsp;
featured heavily in the teaser,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:26.240
with Star-Lord seeming&nbsp;
annoyed with his new friend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:30.160
Thor sports some Ravager-looking clothes and&nbsp;
bids the Guardians farewell as they fly through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:34.640
a portal, resembling one like the space jump&nbsp;
scene from "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2."

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:38.560
The teaser hints that "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;
will see Thor on an emotional journey as he tries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:42.640
to find out who he is and what his purpose&nbsp;
is in this universe. It looks like most of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:47.040
the characters are on a path to self-discovery,&nbsp;
including Valkyrie, who seems rather bored with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:51.840
her leadership role on New Asgard. The peaceful&nbsp;
vibes of the teaser are disrupted at the end when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:56.720
Jane Foster claims Mjolnir, and we get our first&nbsp;
look at Mighty Thor before the clip abruptly ends.

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:01.680
A month later, "Thor: Love and Thunder" got&nbsp;
its first full trailer. With 45 seconds more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.680 --> 00:11:06.640
of content, there was a lot to unpack. While the&nbsp;
teaser was light and airy, the trailer was a tad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:11.040
darker as it gave us the first look at Christian&nbsp;
Bale's menacing villain, Gorr the God Butcher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:15.280
Clearly, this guy has a grudge, but all we know&nbsp;
from what we were shown is that he's creepy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:18.720
has a grudge, and looks like he'll&nbsp;
be a worthy adversary to Thor.

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:22.800
Also stealing the show in the trailer is Jane&nbsp;
Foster, who we only see in Mighty Thor gear and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:27.040
wielding Mjolnir. Thor is totally shocked to&nbsp;
see his ex-girlfriend show up out of nowhere,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.680
let alone holding his beloved hammer, and it's&nbsp;
clear there are still feelings between the two.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:35.200
Valkyrie picks up on this and questions&nbsp;
Thor about what's going on between them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:39.440
Jane's Mighty Thor is also shown summoning&nbsp;
lightning in a mysterious dark hall or cave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:43.280
surrounded by gold statues – some of which&nbsp;
appear to represent important characters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:48.080
from Marvel Comics such as the Living&nbsp;
Tribunal, the Watcher, Infinity, and Death.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:52.080
Additionally, the trailer takes us to Olympus,&nbsp;
where we see Russell Crowe's Zeus for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.600
time. Surrounded by women, the god has&nbsp;
Thor chained to the floor and strips off&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.600 --> 00:11:59.520
all of his clothes, causing an astounding&nbsp;
number of people around Zeus to faint.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.800
There's also a look at Jane competing&nbsp;
in some kind of battle on Olympus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.160
promising both comedy and action in&nbsp;
this particular hall of the gods.

00:12:07.040 --> 00:12:11.040
During the "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;
panel at San Diego Comic-Con in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.360
Taika Waititi revealed that the new movie is&nbsp;
inspired by "The Mighty Thor" comics storyline&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:20.320
from 2015. Written by Jason Aaron, the story&nbsp;
follows Jane Foster as she becomes the Goddess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:24.960
of Thunder after wielding Mjolnir. Tragically,&nbsp;
Jane also has breast cancer at this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:28.720
and every time she holds the hammer and&nbsp;
transforms, the chemotherapy is eradicated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:32.800
from her body. However, Mjolnir will not&nbsp;
eliminate the cancer from her system,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.800 --> 00:12:36.560
meaning she significantly risks death&nbsp;
by continuing to wield the hammer.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.480
Despite knowing that her heroism could lead to&nbsp;
her death, Jane transforms into the Goddess of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.480 --> 00:12:45.600
Thunder one too many times, and she ultimately&nbsp;
dies after defeating Asgardian threat Mangog.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.200
However, after her death, Jane refuses&nbsp;
to go through the gates of Valhalla and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:54.080
is resurrected by Odin. She returns to Earth,&nbsp;
and her cancer eventually goes into remission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:58.480
Could this mean a surprise appearance by&nbsp;
Anthony Hopkins? Odin might be gone in the MCU,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:02.000
but if he meets Jane at the gates&nbsp;
of Valhalla, anything is possible.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:05.840
Jane's cancer storyline may have been confirmed&nbsp;
for "Thor: Love and Thunder" thanks to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:09.760
description of a replica Thor helmet that's&nbsp;
part of the official merchandise for the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.360
The Direct picked up on this subtle&nbsp;
leak, as the helmet's description reads,

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.120
"Suffering from cancer, astrophysicist&nbsp;
and Thor's ex-girlfriend, Jane Foster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:17.120 --> 00:13:19.840
visited New Asgard and her&nbsp;
life was changed forever."

00:13:20.636 --> 00:13:24.160
The Marvel Cinematic Universe timeline –&nbsp;
it's a fickle little sucker that is more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:24.160 --> 00:13:27.920
confusing now than it's ever been. But&nbsp;
whenever a new MCU project comes around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:30.400
we have to figure out where&nbsp;
we're supposed to jam it in.

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:34.000
Thanks to the time jump in "Avengers:&nbsp;
Endgame," the actual Earth that we live on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:38.480
doesn't quite match up with the date&nbsp;
in the MCU. As we reside in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.480
Earth's Mightiest Heroes are&nbsp;
living somewhere in 2024 or 2025.

00:13:42.480 --> 00:13:44.560
However, it might be easier to pin "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.560 --> 00:13:47.520
Love and Thunder" on the timeline&nbsp;
based on what we see in the trailer.

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:50.560
Thanks to the appearance of the Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy, we can assume "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:54.640
Love and Thunder" takes place shortly after the&nbsp;
events of "Avengers: Endgame," when Thor left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:59.040
Earth and the fledgling New Asgard to go on an&nbsp;
adventure with the spacefaring team. A lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.040 --> 00:14:04.160
Phase 4 MCU films happen simultaneously, so "Thor:&nbsp;
Love and Thunder" could very well be occurring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:08.400
during the same time as films like "Shang-Chi&nbsp;
and the Legend of the Ten Rings" or "Eternals."

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:13.760
Being an MCU movie, "Thor: Love and Thunder"&nbsp;
comes with dime-a-dozen fan theories and rumors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:17.040
Since the project was announced, there has&nbsp;
been much speculation about who might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:21.360
popping up in the film. Cameos in the MCU are&nbsp;
extremely hard to keep a secret these days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.280
so if the powers-that-be can pull off a&nbsp;
shocking cameo, our hats are off to them.

00:14:25.280 --> 00:14:28.080
Perhaps the biggest rumored&nbsp;
cameo is that of Ryan Gosling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:28.080 --> 00:14:31.680
who some believe is joining the MCU&nbsp;
based on one lunch Gosling and Taika&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:31.680 --> 00:14:35.600
Waititi were spotted having together before&nbsp;
filming began on "Thor: Love and Thunder".

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.840
Gossip site Just Jared shared photos&nbsp;
of the duo together in August 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.840 --> 00:14:44.080
and fans began speculating who he might play&nbsp;
on Reddit. Beta Ray Bill's name seems to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:48.400
popping up, all via fan theory, but it's&nbsp;
also possible Gosling isn't in this at all.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:52.720
Inverse reported on some rumors, which they&nbsp;
admitted were sketchy, that suggest Jeff Goldblum&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:57.920
will reprise his role as the Grandmaster, and&nbsp;
Rachel House will also be back as Topaz. Also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:02.960
possibly appearing is teeny tiny Throg –&nbsp;
aka Thor, but a frog. We got a glimpse of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:07.280
the amphibian in "Loki" Episode 5, which was&nbsp;
actually a surprise Chris Hemsworth cameo.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:12.000
Speaking of Loki, what about Tom Hiddleston?&nbsp;
We haven't heard anything official. Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:15.120
though he seems to be dead in the timeline&nbsp;
"Thor: Love and Thunder" takes place in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:19.280
you can't count out the God of Mischief&nbsp;
– after all, there are so many of them.

